  "details": "I've noticed while messing with video players that some of the videos I've loaded are more pixelated then they should be. just ran a test and some videos are being loaded at 360X640 instead of 720X1080. youtube has them listed in 720p so i'm not sure if its youtubes side or vrchats.\nSince i can only grab the render texture from avpro i cant directly compare it to the unity player but it looks like the same resolution. \nI've tried changing the maximum resolution value provided on the video player but nothing has changed. from 1080p,720p, and 480p.\nthe provided image is of this video: https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=J9Q3i5w6-Ug \nwhich is one of the videos i was using to test. when i debug the texture size it comes out as 272X640",
